# Melody Masters — environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. With no .env file at all the app runs in
# local-first mode: lessons, instruments, tuner, practice history and settings
# are saved in your browser. Copy to .env.local and fill in only what you need.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# Never commit real keys. None of these are exposed to the browser (no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix), and they are only read in server code.

# --- Optional cross-device profiles (Supabase) -------------------------------
# Leave empty to save progress in each browser only. When set, learners enter
# their name once and can pick it on any device to continue with their progress.
# Setup: run supabase/schema.sql in the Supabase SQL Editor, then copy these from
# Supabase → Project Settings → API (URL) and API Keys (the SECRET key).
# The secret key is only read on the server — never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# (Older projects: the "service_role" key works too, via SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.)

# --- Optional video search ----------------------------------------------------
# Not used by default (the Video Hub ships with a curated, verified list).
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# --- Optional daily practice reminders (Web Push) ------------------------------
# Needs Supabase above. Generate keys once:  node scripts/generate-vapid-keys.mjs
# then run supabase/migrations/003_push_subscriptions.sql in the Supabase SQL Editor.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Contact for the push service: mailto:you@example.com or https://your-site
VAPID_SUBJECT=
# Protects /api/push/cron (Vercel Cron sends it automatically as a Bearer token).
CRON_SECRET=
